# The deck's identity and pairing (#180, CYBERDECKS.md §9; deck/os/README.md "Pairing"): `deck-link run` asks
# scutoons.com for access with the deck's own key (/var/lib/deck/identity, made at first boot – deck-firstboot), keeps the
# code to pair with and, once a member approved the deck on the account page, its ~1 h token in /run/deck-link (2750
# root:deck, tmpfiles.d): the stage's splash shows the code + QR, the stage and deck-tls send the token. Revoked or
# expired → a new code, by itself. Root, so the private key stays 0600 root; the user deck only reads the run directory.
[Unit]
Description=SCUTOONS deck link (identity, pairing, the deck token)
# not After=network-online.target: it retries by itself offline, and the boot's network comes later (#251)
After=deck-firstboot.service

[Service]
ExecStart=/usr/bin/deck-link run
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
UMask=0027

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
